!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/invalid/a-mark-before-a-declared-application-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §12.1, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.10"
  description: """
    A declared application is substitution and nothing more: `x` is `box`'s record with `text` in place of `T`, and
    its `extension` is the head's (§5.10), so `f: x` and `f: box<text>` are two types of one shape. The mark is sugar
    for a record definition's `extension` and §12.1 admits it before a record body, a composition or a subtraction
    alone, so before an application it is a parse error at the mark. To make every application abstract, mark the
    parametric record, `box => abstract <T> { v: T }`; to make one, declare a record composing the application,
    `x => abstract box<text> & {}`.
    """
  error: {
    category: resolver
  }
}
